---
interface Props {
  /** Button label, from the shared `solutions.disclosure.*` nouns. */
  triggerLabel: string;
  /** Unique per mount: a popover needs an id, and two on one page must not collide. */
  popId: string;
  techDiff: {
    overline: string;
    title: string;
    description: string;
    traditionalLabel: string;
    rediaccLabel: string;
    rows: { traditional: string; rediacc: string }[];
  };
}

const { techDiff, triggerLabel, popId } = Astro.props;
const titleId = `${popId}-title`;
---

<section class="sp-tech-detail">
  <div class="sp-tech-detail-inner">
    <div class="sp-overline">{techDiff.overline}</div>
    <h2>{techDiff.title}</h2>
    <p>{techDiff.description}</p>

    {/* A real <table>, not a CSS grid, and the labels are repeated INSIDE every
        cell for the single-column collapse.

        The grid version carried column identity in grid POSITION alone. Below
        768px `solution-pages.css` collapses it to one column, so the two headers
        stayed at the top and every cell under them became unlabelled: measured at
        390px, 10 cells against exactly ONE "traditional" and ONE "rediacc"
        header. The only surviving cue was a 20%-alpha tint, which is not one.

        `SPComparisonTable.astro` next door was already a proper table, so this is
        adopting the sibling that works rather than patching the media query.

        The per-cell label is `aria-hidden`: `<th scope="col">` already gives
        assistive tech the association at every width, so this span is purely the
        visual half and must not be announced twice. It adds no i18n keys - both
        strings are the ones the header row already renders. */}
    {/* NATIVE POPOVER, not a React island. This component is static Astro, and adding
        React to get a dialog would ship a runtime for a table. `popover="auto"` gives
        light-dismiss, Escape and top-layer stacking from the platform, and the pattern is
        already on this page: SolutionConstellation.astro:289 does exactly this.
        WITHOUT JS the button is inert and the table stays in the DOM, so a crawler and a
        no-script visitor still get the whole comparison. */}
    <button type="button" class="sp-disclosure-trigger" popovertarget={popId}>
      {triggerLabel}
    </button>

    <div class="sp-disclosure-pop" id={popId} popover="auto" role="dialog" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <h3 class="sp-disclosure-pop-title" id={titleId}>{techDiff.title}</h3>
    <table class="sp-tech-detail-compare">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="sp-tech-detail-col-header traditional">{techDiff.traditionalLabel}</th>
          <th scope="col" class="sp-tech-detail-col-header rediacc">{techDiff.rediaccLabel}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {techDiff.rows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="sp-tech-detail-cell">
              <span class="sp-tech-detail-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">{techDiff.traditionalLabel}</span>
              {row.traditional}
            </td>
            <td class="sp-tech-detail-cell">
              <span class="sp-tech-detail-cell-label" aria-hidden="true">{techDiff.rediaccLabel}</span>
              {row.rediacc}
            </td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
